# Intro - Control Structures - Decision and Repetition

When you write a C++ program, the computer normally reads and executes your code from top to bottom. However, real programs need to make decisions and repeat actions. This is where control structures become essential.&#x20;

By the end of this unit, you will be about to write programs that can check conditions, loop through tasks, and control the flow of execution with confidence. These skills are fundamental and will be used in every C++ program you write.&#x20;

What's more, after you learning this unit, you may can try to make your own text based game.&#x20;

